privacyfox (0.1.4) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Real, deterministic fix for the install-time "keep built-in
    blocker?" dialog -- supersedes 0.1.3's speculative attempt
    (dismissedExtensionInstallWarnings), which is removed as
    redundant now that the actual root cause is fixed properly.

    Traced the exact guard logic in Waterfox's own source
    (WaterfoxBlockerExtensionDetector.sys.mjs): every one of its
    detection/notification/install-warning functions checks
    waterfox.blocker.coexist FIRST, unconditionally, before touching
    anything else -- when true, they all return immediately. Setting
    it via policy (locked true) means none of that machinery ever
    runs at all, rather than racing a value it reads elsewhere. The
    native blocker itself stays genuinely, permanently off via the
    separately-locked waterfox.blocker.enabled -- this just also
    stops Waterfox's own nanny-logic from reacting to that at all.

    Real user testing (multiple rounds, working through this
    together) is what surfaced this needed a real fix rather than
    being documented away as cosmetic -- a public tool showing
    unexplained warnings on first launch, that LibreWolf/Waterfox
    themselves never show, undermines trust regardless of whether the
    underlying protection already works.

 -- PrivacyFox Project <hello@privacyfox.dev>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:27:22 -0500

privacyfox (0.1.3) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Attempt to suppress Waterfox's install-time "keep built-in
    blocker?" dialog for uBlock Origin by preemptively setting
    waterfox.blocker.dismissedExtensionInstallWarnings via policy.
    Honest caveat: this may hit the exact same startup-timing race
    that let the dialog through in the first place (both prefs apply
    via the same Preferences policy mechanism, at the same moment) --
    worth trying since it's low-cost, not guaranteed to fully resolve
    it. Confirmed real-world testing showed the underlying protection
    already works correctly even when the dialog appears (the
    built-in blocker stays locked off regardless of which button
    gets clicked) -- this only targets the cosmetic dialog itself.

 -- PrivacyFox Project <hello@privacyfox.dev>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 11:08:04 -0500

privacyfox (0.1.2) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Disable Waterfox's native ad-blocking engine entirely via policy
    (waterfox.blocker.enabled/ui.enabled, locked false), in favor of
    the force-installed uBlock Origin extension. Previously relied on
    Waterfox's own automatic extension-conflict detection to sort
    this out reactively after install, which left a leftover toolbar
    indicator and an unexplained prompt. Fixing it at the policy
    level, before first launch, is the correct root-cause fix.

 -- PrivacyFox Project <hello@privacyfox.dev>  Tue, 15 Sep 2026 09:58:48 -0500

privacyfox (0.1.1) unstable; urgency=medium

